# Call-site ledger of dagster-pipes 1.13.28 (sdist, SHA-256 f785c2ee...).
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# The analysed source is dagster_pipes/__init__.py and dagster_pipes/version.py
# (requires-python >=3.10,<3.15). dagster-pipes.md shows how this ledger
# applies the scope rules A, B1-B5 and C. In short:
# - The abstract classes (abc) are PipesContextLoader, PipesLogWriterChannel,
#   PipesLogWriter, PipesMessageWriter, PipesMessageWriterChannel,
#   PipesParamsLoader, PipesBlobStoreMessageWriter,
#   PipesBlobStoreMessageWriterChannel, PipesStdioLogWriter and
#   PipesStdioLogWriterChannel. They are no receivers; every concrete package
#   subclass overrides each of their abstract methods.
# - The roles (B2, by annotation): a message writer (PipesMessageWriter) is
#   one of PipesDefaultMessageWriter, the five blob store writers (S3, GCS,
#   Azure, DBFS, Unity Catalog Volumes) and PipesPrefectLogsMessageWriter; a
#   message channel (PipesMessageWriterChannel) is one of the four blob store
#   channels (which inherit write_message), PipesFileMessageWriterChannel,
#   PipesStreamMessageWriterChannel, PipesBufferedStreamMessageWriterChannel
#   and PipesPrefectLogsMessageWriterChannel; a context loader is one of the
#   six concrete loaders; a params loader is PipesMappingParamsLoader (and
#   PipesEnvVarParamsLoader), PipesCliArgsParamsLoader or
#   PipesDatabricksNotebookWidgetsParamsLoader.
# - params (PipesParams, an abstract Mapping) is the dict that decode_param
#   (json) makes when the package passes it, or a client mapping (opaque, B5).
# - The S3 and Azure clients and the Databricks widgets are annotated Any,
#   which states no type, so their docstrings decide (judgement 3): the
#   Azure client is a BlobServiceClient, the S3 client is boto3.client("s3");
#   the widgets' docstring names no class. The GCS client is annotated
#   google.cloud.storage.Client. google-cloud-storage, azure-storage-blob,
#   boto3 and pyspark are not installed and are named as missing modules
#   (judgements 4 and 5).
# - A call of a method decorated with @contextmanager runs
#   contextlib.contextmanager.helper, which calls the generator function back.
default reject dagster_pipes.PipesContext.__enter__, dagster_pipes.PipesContext.__exit__: no with statement in the package enters a PipesContext; its items are files from the builtin open, a tempfile wrapper, ExitStacks, a contextlib.nullcontext, the _GeneratorContextManager objects of the package's @contextmanager methods, and the blob clients of the client's Azure client
default reject dagster_pipes.PipesContext.get: the receiver of this get is not the class PipesContext: it is a dict (the params that decode_param or json makes, a message's params, an exception dict), a queue.Queue, the client's widgets object or a pyspark configuration; only PipesContext.get() in open_dagster_pipes (1637:32) accepts it
default reject dagster_pipes.PipesContext.set: this set is threading.Event.set or the builtin set(); only PipesContext.set(context) in open_dagster_pipes (1647:21) accepts it
default reject dagster_pipes.ExcThread.join: the receiver of this join is a str separator, os.path, a plain threading.Thread (693:28) or super() in ExcThread.join, which skips ExcThread; only thread.join() in PipesStdioLogWriterChannel.capture (870:28), on the ExcThread of line 850, accepts it

